<title>SWEDEN: Skandia sells holdings in Iceland.</title>
<headline>Skandia sells holdings in Iceland.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurer Skandia on Tuesday said it would sell all its holdings in insurance companies in Iceland to Vatryggingafelag Island hf (VIS).</p>
<p>&quot;The sale will have a positive effect on Skandia's result and net asset value,&quot; Skandia said in a statement.</p>
<p>No financial details were disclosed.</p>
<p>Skandia said its operations in Iceland had gained market share in recent years and reported improved profitability.</p>
<p>Vatryggingafelag has a prominent position in the Icelandic life assurance and non-life insurance market and will derive synergies through integrating the respective units of the companies, it said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
